## Can OpenCode Replace Pi Stack?

### **TL;DR: NO - Not a Drop-in Replacement**

| Aspect | Pi Stack | OpenCode | Compatible? |
|--------|----------|----------|-------------|
| **Language** | TypeScript/Node.js | Go | ❌ No |
| **Architecture** | Library/SDK | Standalone binary | ❌ No |
| **Session Storage** | JSONL files | SQLite database | ❌ No |
| **Integration** | Programmatic API | CLI/RPC only | ⚠️ Limited |
| **Session Management** | `SessionManager` class | Internal DB layer | ❌ No |
| **Model Registry** | `ModelRegistry` + `discoverModels()` | Internal config | ❌ No |
| **Tool System** | TypeBox schemas + executors | Go structs + handlers | ❌ No |
| **OAuth Flow** | Built-in `getOAuthApiKey()` | Config-based | ⚠️ Different |
| **Extensibility** | TypeScript hooks/tools/skills | MCP + custom commands | ⚠️ Different paradigm |

### **Why They're Incompatible**

#### 1. **Runtime Mismatch**
Clawdis is a **Node.js TypeScript** application. OpenCode is a **Go binary**. You cannot import OpenCode modules into TypeScript.

**Evidence** ([clawdis imports](https://github.com/steipete/clawdis/blob/main/src/agents/pi-embedded-runner.ts#L16-L24)):
```typescript
import {
  buildSystemPrompt,
  createAgentSession,
  discoverAuthStorage,
  // ... TypeScript modules, not Go packages
} from "@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent";
```

#### 2. **API Surface Incompatibility**

**Pi's programmatic API**:
```typescript
const authStorage = discoverAuthStorage(agentDir);
const modelRegistry = discoverModels(authStorage, agentDir);
const { session } = await createAgentSession({
  sessionManager: SessionManager.open(sessionDir),
  authStorage,
  modelRegistry,
  tools: createClawdisCodingTools(cwd),
});
```

**OpenCode has NO equivalent TypeScript API**. It's a CLI tool with RPC mode ([docs](https://github.com/opencode-ai/opencode/blob/73ee493265acf15fcd8caab2bc8cd3bd375b63cb/README.md#rpc-mode)):
```bash
opencode --mode rpc --no-session
# Send JSON over stdin
{"type":"prompt","message":"List files"}
```

#### 3. **Session Storage Incompatibility**

**Pi**: JSONL files with tree structure ([clawdis session dir](https://github.com/steipete/clawdis/blob/main/docs/agent.md)):
```
~/.clawdis/sessions/*.jsonl
```

**OpenCode**: SQLite database ([config docs](https://github.com/opencode-ai/opencode/blob/73ee493265acf15fcd8caab2bc8cd3bd375b63cb/README.md#configuration-file-structure)):
```json
{
  "data": {
    "directory": ".opencode"  // SQLite DB location
  }
}
```

#### 4. **Tool System Incompatibility**

**Pi tools** ([source](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/a07347755550632ace6ac1fd16196a9fdbabd51d/packages/coding-agent/src/core/tools/bash.ts)):
```typescript
import type { AgentTool, AgentToolResult } from "@mariozechner/pi-ai";

export const bashTool: AgentTool = {
  name: "bash",
  parameters: Type.Object({
    command: Type.String({ description: "Command to execute" })
  }),
  execute: async (params) => { /* TypeScript implementation */ }
};
```

**OpenCode tools** ([source](https://github.com/opencode-ai/opencode/blob/73ee493265acf15fcd8caab2bc8cd3bd375b63cb/internal/llm/tools.go)):
```go
type Tool struct {
    Name        string
    Description string
    Parameters  json.RawMessage
}
// Go implementation, not callable from TypeScript
```

